前途的，我劝你还是争取想办法读个专科，或者学门正经的专业，免得以后一直只能在工地干活”，张澈一副领导的口吻道。林飞随口道：“算了吧，我也没什么大志向，也不指望当官发财，过几年凑合着找房媳妇儿，能过日子就行了。真要没人看得上，自己一个人也不至于饿死。”柳景岚笑吟吟道：“林飞，没想到你年纪轻轻的，心态挺悠哉的，你这样倒是知足常乐。”“知足肯定是不知足的，总想吃点好吃的，住得也好点，但常乐倒是真的”，林飞掏出自己的大前门软包，抽出一根，敬给张澈，“来一根？”张澈皱眉，这种几毛钱一根的香烟都敬给自己？当自己跟你一样是饥不择食的穷烟鬼？“不用了，我一般只抽古巴进口的雪茄，而且这里有女士，不方便抽烟”，张澈很温柔地看了眼柳景岚。林飞问向柳景岚，“柳姐不介意吧？”“叫我景岚就成了，你都跟我爸平辈论交，还叫我姐算什么”，柳景岚白了他一眼，道，“抽吧，不过少抽点，快吃饭了”。一旁的张澈眼里一阵愠色，竟然让这么一个没用的穷小子叫他喜欢的女人的名字，简直是玷污！但柳景岚都这么说了，他也不好强行干涉。想了想，他眼里露出几分得意，朗声说道：“小林啊，我们夏国古人有说过一句话，叫‘淡泊是高风，太枯则无以济人利物’。你没什么文化，可能无法理解，这句话的意思是说，把功名利禄看得很淡，本是一种高尚情*，但如过分清心寡欲，就对社会人生少有贡献。现在很多社会上的年轻人跟你一样，用看似随意的态度，无所谓的态度，去面对人生，自己把自己当作高尚的隐士，无所谓这些事业与名利。但实际上，男子汉大丈夫，活在世上如果连这点志向都没有，那就等于白来世间走了一遭，也是没责任心的表现。我劝你，还是好好学习，多长点知识文化，是吧，景岚？”他的话一语双关，看起来像劝解林飞，但也同时是认为林飞在装清高，压根是没本事创出一番事业。张澈说完，下意识地就看向一旁的柳景岚，他觉得自己的引经据典，必然能以才情来吸引柳景岚这种书卷气的女子，连他自己都觉得自己帅呆了。柳景岚也很配合，点头“嗯”了一声，“学长说得也有道理。”张澈心里一喜，果然，征服这种内心清高的美女，还是得靠自己的满腹经纶。“哦？学长还看过《菜根谭》？现在人知道三字经，道德经的倒是多，但知道和去读《菜根谭》的，倒是少了”，林飞有些意外地笑了笑，看来这个家伙不是纯粹公子哥，还是真正读过些书。《菜根谭》，是元末明初道人洪应明，所撰写的一部，教人为人处事的儒家经典。用各种看似随意的语录，随笔，来讲述人生的真谛。刚刚还得意地笑着的张澈，忽然脸色一僵，半张着嘴，不可思议地转头看着林飞。“你……你怎么知道的？你读过？”张澈根本不敢相信，这种工地搬砖，四处找工作，连个文凭都没的家伙，会读过这种儒家经典。毕竟这也不是什么常见的通俗读物。可林飞却是点了点头，吐了口白烟，悠然道：“看过一点，我记得里面有句话，叫‘宠辱不惊，闲看庭前花开花落；去留无意，漫随天外云卷云舒。’荣耀还是屈辱，这些都不是太重要，用安静的心情，欣赏庭院中花开花落。对于所有浮沉和得失，都可以淡然处之，笑看天上云彩随风聚散。我觉得，这句话在我身上比较合适，我也不是说没责任，没担当，只不过看淡了一些东西，自然也就不是太在意了。人各有志，不可强求，张学长，你说呢？”看着林飞那憨厚的笑容，张澈却是额头出了点冷汗，心里一阵憋闷，本来是露一手给柳景岚瞧瞧，顺便把林飞说得哑口无言。没想到，反而是帮林飞做嫁衣，用同一部书里的语句反驳了自己。这就好像是他在班门弄斧，还说人家不知道，人家根本就一清二楚，只是没跟你一样显摆而已！一时间，张澈感觉自己的耳根有些发烫，这可丢人了……柳景岚果然也显得颇为惊讶，“没想到林飞你还挺有文化啊，看来是读过不少书，怪不得年纪轻轻有这份心境。”“也就瞎读了些，谈不上有文化，但做人的道理还是明白的”，林飞道。“至少我读过，但我背不出里面的这些经典段落”。柳景岚浅浅笑着，像是一朵盛开的娇嫩百合，让一旁的张澈真是又气又喜欢，气的是这不是为他而笑，喜欢的是……这女人实在越看越美。京城那些所谓的名媛闺秀，跟这个女人比，简直是绿叶衬红花。", "source": "www.quanwenyuedu.io", "source_url": "https://www.quanwenyuedu.io/n/nuzongcaideshenjibaobiao/10.html", "_fixed": true, "content_en": "Chapter 0010 Watching flowers in the garden Liu Jinglan said helplessly: \"Mom, you are overthinking. I haven't agreed to the senior yet, and I don't want to get married for the time being.\" \"If you don't want to get married, you can fall in love first, you stone-headed girl!\" Yu Meimei hates women. \"It's okay, Auntie. I believe that with my sincerity, I will be able to move Jing Lan. At least this time she is willing to let me come here to see you two,\" Zhang Che said with an elegant expression. Yu Meimei said cheerfully, \"Yes, yes, it can be done. I'll go in and make two more dishes, and then we can start dinner. You guys chat first. Jing Lan remembers to pour tea for Xiao Zhang and Lin Fei.\" As soon as Meimei left, the scene turned cold. Zhang Che glanced at Lin Fei and found that Lin Fei had been silent since just now. He was watching the news on TV silently, drinking tea, and seemed to have heard nothing. He couldn't help but feel slightly dissatisfied. \"Xiao Lin, you may not have read any books, but you are young and have no future if you keep doing menial jobs. I advise you to try to find a way to get a junior college or learn a serious major, so as not to have to work on the construction site in the future,\" Zhang Che said in a leader's tone. Lin Fei said casually: \"Forget it, I don't have any big ambitions, and I don't expect to be an official and make a fortune. In a few years, I will find a house and a wife, and I can live a good life. If no one really cares about me, I won't starve to death by myself.\" Liu Jinglan smiled and said: \"Lin Fei, I didn't expect that you are so young and have such a leisurely attitude. \"Yes, you are contented.\" \"Being contented is definitely not enough. You always want to eat something delicious and live better, but Chang Le is real.\" Lin Fei took out his big front door soft bag, took out one, and offered it to Zhang Che, \"One?\" Zhang Che frowned, would you give this kind of cigarettes that only cost a few cents to you? Do you think I am a poor smoker like you? \"No, I usually only smoke cigars imported from Cuba, and there are ladies here, so it's not convenient to smoke.\" Zhang Che glanced at Liu Jinglan tenderly. Lin Fei asked Liu Jinglan, \"Sister Liu, don't you mind?\" \"Just call me Jinglan. You're already on the same level as my dad, so why call me sister?\" Liu Jinglan rolled her eyes at him and said, \"Smoking, but less, it's time to eat.\" Zhang Che, who was standing by, had a look of anger in his eyes. It was such a defilement to let such a useless poor boy call the name of the woman he liked! But Liu Jinglan said so, so it was not easy for him to interfere forcefully. After thinking about it, he showed a bit of pride in his eyes and said loudly: \"Xiao Lin, our ancients in the Xia Kingdom once said, 'Indifferent is a high wind, and if it is too dry, it will not help people and things.' You have no education, so you may not be able to understand the meaning of this sentence. What I mean is that it is a noble sentiment to take fame and wealth very lightly, but if you are too pure and have few desires, you will have little contribution to social life. Many young people in society are like you, with a seemingly casual attitude and an indifferent attitude. When facing life, I regard myself as a noble hermit who doesn't care about career, fame and fortune. But in fact, if a man doesn't even have this ambition in the world, it is equivalent to living in this world in vain, and he has no responsibility. The expression of the heart. I advise you to study hard and gain more knowledge, right, Jing Lan?\" His words were pun-intended, and he seemed to be trying to persuade Lin Fei, but at the same time, he thought that Lin Fei was pretending to be aloof and had no ability to create a career. After Zhang Che finished speaking, he subconsciously looked at Liu Jinglan aside. He felt that his citation of scriptures would definitely attract a bookish woman like Liu Jinglan with his talent. Even he himself felt that he was extremely handsome. Liu Jinglan was also very cooperative, nodding \"Yeah\" and saying, \"Senior, what you said makes sense.\" Zhang Che felt happy. Sure enough, to conquer such a noble beauty, you still have to rely on your own experience. \"Oh? Senior, have you read \"Cai Gen Tan\"? Nowadays, more people know the Three Character Classic and the Tao Te Ching, but there are fewer people who know and read \"Cai Gen Tan\".\" Lin Fei smiled in surprise. It seems that this guy is not just a young man, but has actually read some books. \"Cai Gen Tan\" is a Confucian classic written by Hong Yingming, a Taoist in the late Yuan and early Ming dynasties, which teaches people how to behave. Use various seemingly random quotations and essays to tell the true meaning of life. Zhang Che, who had been smiling proudly just now, suddenly stiffened, opened his mouth half-open, and turned his head to look at Lin Fei in disbelief. \"You...how do you know? Have you read it?\" Zhang Che simply couldn't believe that a guy like this who was carrying bricks on a construction site, looking for jobs everywhere, and didn't even have a diploma could have read such a Confucian classic. After all, this is not a common popular reading. But Lin Fei nodded, blew out the white smoke, and said leisurely: \"I read it a little bit, and I remember there is a saying in it, which is: 'Don't be surprised by favor or disgrace, just watch the flowers blooming and falling in front of the court; you have no intention of leaving or leaving, just let the clouds roll and relax in the sky.' Glory or humiliation, these are not too important. Use a quiet mood to appreciate the flowers blooming and falling in the courtyard. You can deal with all ups and downs, gains and losses indifferently, and watch the clouds in the sky gather with the wind with a smile. I think this sentence is more suitable for me. I am not saying that I am not responsible, but I have taken some things lightly, so I don't care too much. Everyone has their own ambitions, so don't force it, what do you think?\" Looking at Lin Fei's honest smile, Zhang Che felt a little cold on his forehead and felt depressed. He originally showed his hand to Liu Jinglan, which made Lin Fei speechless. Unexpectedly, he helped Lin Fei make wedding clothes and refuted himself with sentences from the same book. It's like he's playing tricks on the class and saying that others don't know. They know everything about it, but they just don't show it off like you do! For a moment, Zhang Che felt that the roots of his ears were a little hot, which is embarrassing... Liu Jinglan also looked quite surprised, \"I didn't expect you, Lin Fei, to be quite educated. It seems like", "title_en": "Chapter 10"}